%N A399398 Triangle read by rows: T(n,k) is the number of spanning trees in the k-twisted n X n torus grid graph, 0 <= k < n.
%C A399398 The graph is obtained from the n X n cylinder graph by adding edges between the two boundary circles with a circular shift of k. More precisely, if we let the vertices of the graph be (i,j) for i,j in Z/nZ, the edges are {(i,j),(i+1,j)} for 0 <= i,j < n, {(i,j),(i,j+1)} for 0 <= i < n, 0 <= j < n-1, and {(i,n-1),(i+k,0)} for 0 <= i < n.
%C A399398 Multiple edges which appear for n = 2 are taken into account.
%H A399398 Gareth Branwyn and George Hart, <a href="https://makezine.com/article/science/math-monday-the-twisted-torus/">Math Monday: The twisted torus</a>, Make: Magazine, 2010.
%H A399398 Qiang Dong and Juan Zhao, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tcs.2024.114610">The diameter of rectangular twisted torus</a>, Theoretical Computer Science 1003 (2024), article 114610.
%F A399398 T(n,k) = T(n,n-k) for 1 <= k <= n-1.
